        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beverley Knight, Sam Cooke, Aretha Franklin\n- Roles: recording artist, radio presenter, musical theatre actress, singer, songwriter, entrepreneur\n- Products: The B-Funk, studio albums\n- Topics: American soul music\n\nFacts:\n- Sam Cooke was an American singer, songwriter, and entrepreneur who was born on January 22, 1931, and died on December 11, 1964.\n- Beverley Knight was born Beverley Anne Smith on March 22, 1973.\n- Beverley Knight is an English recording artist, radio presenter, and musical theatre actress.\n- Beverley Knight released her debut album, \"The B-Funk,\" in 1995.\n- Beverley Knight was heavily influenced by American soul music icons such as Sam Cooke and Aretha Franklin.\n- Beverley Knight has released eight studio albums to date.",
